cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Benchmarking Latency-Sensitive Network Protocols: code, scripts and data"
abstract: >-
  Artifact for the paper "Benchmarking Latency-Sensitive Network Protocols:
  A Reproducible Methodology for Sub-Millisecond Measurements". Contains the
  game_sockets Rust library (UDP, TCP, QUIC and GameNetworkingSockets behind
  one game-style API), the echo server, traffic-generating client and
  statistics tools, the Bash/Python scripts that set up network namespaces,
  netem and CPU isolation and run the test matrix, and the raw per-packet
  data: 400-run matrices (4 protocols x 10 network scenarios x 10 runs) for
  the optimized, unoptimized-loopback and unoptimized-veth configurations,
  plus 30-run QUIC validation sets.
